'16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 28, 2008 at 12:15 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8549002831307773554</id><published>2008-09-27T19:49:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-09-27T19:49:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>UNnewglobalfinancialorder&quot;26 September 2008 – The ...</title><content type='html'>&lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.un.org/apps/news/story.asp?NewsID=28300&amp;Cr=general+assembly&amp;Cr1=debate&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;UNnewglobalfinancialorder&lt;/A&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&quot;26 September 2008 – The Prime Minister of the United Kingdom today called for a new global financial system to bring an end to the current economic turmoil, laying out five principles on which the order should be based as he addressed the General Assembly’s annual high-level debate.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;“This has been an era of global prosperity. It has been an era also of global turbulence,” Gordon Brown said at United Nations Headquarters in New York.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;To bring an end to the culture of irresponsibility, “we must now build a new global financial order founded on transparency, not opacity; rewarding success, not excess; responsibility, not impunity; and which is global, not national.”&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;IMAGINE THAT!!!</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/8549002831307773554'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/8549002831307773554'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html?showComment=1222566540000#c8549002831307773554' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 27, 2008 at 7:49 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-2683575483939094362</id><published>2008-09-27T13:56:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-09-27T13:56:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Things are looking ugly, but there&#39;s something we ...</title><content type='html'>Things are looking ugly, but there&#39;s something we should all remember, even though it&#39;s difficult at times: the State isn&#39;t in control of everything. The State can never harm the most precious thing you have: your immortal soul. Christ told us he  would look out for us. That we are more valuable than many sparrows. We may be headed for the biggest upheaval in the history of the world, but you must remember these three things: 1. This world isn&#39;t it. 2. God loves you more than you love yourself. 3. He will never allow you to be tested beyond your strength. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Let&#39;s march into the coming crisis together, with a cool head, with faith in Him, and trust in his providence. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Peace,&lt;BR/&gt;            -Sans Authoritas</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/2683575483939094362'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/2683575483939094362'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html?showComment=1222545360000#c2683575483939094362' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 27, 2008 at 1:56 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-1250928134664932574</id><published>2008-09-27T12:54:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-09-27T12:54:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>I think the idea that the video games are a player...</title><content type='html'>I think the idea that the video games are a player in this is a non-starter.  I&#39;ve been playing them for years and i do not feel any more likely to take an innocent life (under orders or not) than I would be otherwise.  What HAS changed me, however, is my ever expanding knowledge of politics and history.  Sparked in no small part to Mr. Grigg himself as we spent time together touring the U.S. in college...many years ago.  No, I would not take an innocent life, even under orders.  I do, however, posses the tools, skills, and willingness to take the life of anyone who attempts harm upon any member of my family whether through direct action or conspiracy to deprive them of their liberties.  Until we all are willing to do the same, the march of ever expanding tyranny will continue.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/1250928134664932574'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/1250928134664932574'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html?showComment=1222541640000#c1250928134664932574' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 27, 2008 at 12:54 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-536637600261989687</id><published>2008-09-27T12:50:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-09-27T12:50:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Isn&#39;t it odd how unguided, mystical, Hegelian hist...</title><content type='html'>Isn&#39;t it odd how unguided, mystical, Hegelian historical forces seem to move us inexorably toward the creation of a despotic police state with its monopoly of force via an &#39;internal security force&#39; backed up by international peacekeepers, if needed, as outlined in Lincoln P. Bloomfield&#39;s 1961 State Department funded study &#39;Memorandum No. 7: A World Effectively Controlled By The United Nations&#39;? &quot;Guided evolution&quot; indeed.      -RW</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/536637600261989687'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/536637600261989687'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html?showComment=1222541400000#c536637600261989687' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 27, 2008 at 12:50 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8811660903224685248</id><published>2008-09-27T09:21:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-09-27T09:21:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>&quot;The sinkhole of dictatorial abuse and Sicilian co...</title><content type='html'>&quot;The sinkhole of dictatorial abuse and Sicilian corruption described by Bill is a small community in South Dakota -- that haven of sober Midwestern rectitude whose citizens aren&#39;t afflicted with a state income tax. If it&#39;s this bad in the green wood, what&#39;s it like in the dry? Well, according to Bill, &quot;these abuses do, sadly, happen in almost every town in America.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;This is the kind of breathtaking, eye-opening investigative journalism that used to be done in the Mainstream Media ... 40 years ago, before it fell under consolidated Corpgov ownership.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Frankly, Will&#39;s &quot;Rubicon in the Rear-View, Part I&quot; essay is painful to read. Part II looms like a chemotherapy apppointment. But closing one&#39;s eyes and clicking to a happier webpage won&#39;t make these ugly facts go away.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Both the unfolding economic collapse, and the militarized law enforcement empowered to Taser the restless hordes of jobless and homeless into submission, suggest serious potential for social unrest ahead.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;You gotta love the historical irony: just as US-style fiat-money democracy was being administered globally at gunpoint as the &#39;ne plus ultra&#39; of politico-economic systems, it spectacularly crashed in flames. Death to the dollar ...</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/8811660903224685248'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/8811660903224685248'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html?showComment=1222528860000#c8811660903224685248' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 27, 2008 at 9:21 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4636466329500501721</id><published>2008-09-26T15:34:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2008-09-26T15:34:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Zachary,Who is behind it?  The same globalists and...</title><content type='html'>Zachary,&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Who is behind it?  The same globalists and Free Traitors who are behind most of the corporate fascism we see today.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Why are they doing it? They KNOW that they are begging for a revolution.  This is an effort to protect themselves from an angry populace that comes to realize they have been ripped off.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/4636466329500501721'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/7010630768189355318/comments/default/4636466329500501721'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html?showComment=1222464840000#c4636466329500501721' title=''/><author><name>Mark</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/09/rubicon-in-rear-view-part-i.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7010630768189355318' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/7010630768189355318' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 26, 2008 at 3:34 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-637950592580